<!-- ============================== THE PREMISE ============================= -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first">
    <p class="kicker">Begin Here</p>
    <h2>Three Questions, Routinely Confused</h2>
    <p class="lede">Almost every argument about aliens is actually three arguments wearing one coat. Separate
    them and the fog clears immediately.</p>

    <ol class="biblio">
      <li><strong>Is there life elsewhere?</strong> <span class="sci">◆</span> An astrobiological question, approached with telescopes and chemistry. Unresolved, actively advancing, and the odds look better every decade.</li>
      <li><strong>Has anything intelligent reached Earth?</strong> <span class="spec">◆</span> A question of physical evidence. Here the record is enormous, chaotic, and — after eighty years — still without a single object, sample or image that survives expert handling.</li>
      <li><strong>What would contact <em>mean</em>?</strong> <span class="myth">◆</span> A philosophical and spiritual question, the oldest of the three, and the one the channelled literature actually addresses.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>You can hold a confident answer to the first, agnosticism on the second and deep interest in the third
    without a single contradiction. Most people instead let the appeal of question three do the work of
    answering question two, and that is where the discipline is lost.</p>

    <p class="muted small">Grading throughout: <span class="sci">◆ established science</span> ·
    <span class="hist">◆ scholarship and history</span> · <span class="spec">◆ speculative and contested</span> ·
    <span class="myth">◆ myth, tradition and primary esoteric text</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<!-- ============================== THE PLATES ============================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Eight Plates</p>
    <h2>The State of the Question</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">From the chemistry of worlds to the anatomy of an encounter.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate I <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Worlds Are There</h3>
      <p>In 1992 humanity knew of no planet outside this solar system. The confirmed count is now past 5,800,
      and the statistics of the Kepler survey imply that planets are the ordinary consequence of star
      formation, not the exception.</p>
      <p>Perhaps one in five Sun-like stars carries a roughly Earth-sized world in the liquid-water zone. In
      this galaxy alone that is billions of candidate surfaces, and there are two trillion galaxies. The
      shortage of real estate, which was a serious objection in 1960, is gone.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Mayor and Queloz took the 2019 Nobel for 51 Pegasi b. What remains unknown is not
      whether the worlds exist but whether chemistry crosses into biology easily or almost never.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate II <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Drake Equation Is a Confession</h3>
      <p>Drake's 1961 formula multiplies seven terms to estimate the number of communicating civilisations.
      The first three are now measured rather well. The last four — how often life starts, how often it becomes
      intelligent, how often that builds a transmitter, and how long such a thing lasts — are each uncertain by
      many orders of magnitude.</p>
      <p>Multiply those uncertainties together and the honest output spans from "we are the only ones" to
      "millions". The equation's real value was never the number. It was in laying out exactly which
      ignorances stand between us and the answer.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate III <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>Fermi's Question Still Stands</h3>
      <p>At lunch in Los Alamos in 1950, Fermi asked: <em>where is everybody?</em> The galaxy is around 13
      billion years old. Even at a crawling one percent of lightspeed, a patient civilisation could cross it in
      a few tens of millions of years — an eyeblink. The sky should be busy. It is silent.</p>
      <p>The proposed resolutions are a map of our anxieties. A Great Filter behind us, meaning life or
      intelligence is vanishingly rare; a filter ahead, meaning technological species reliably destroy
      themselves; the zoo hypothesis, that we are deliberately left alone; the dark forest, that broadcasting
      is suicidal; or simply that we have searched a laughably small volume for a laughably short time.</p>
      <p class="muted small">All remain live. None is established. The silence is real data and nobody knows
      what it means.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate IV <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>How We Are Actually Looking</h3>
      <p>Radio SETI has listened since Drake's Project Ozma in 1960; Breakthrough Listen now surveys a million
      nearby stars. Nothing has ever repeated. The 1977 "Wow!" signal lasted 72 seconds and has never returned
      despite hundreds of re-examinations.</p>
      <p>The sharper tool is now spectroscopy. JWST can read the atmosphere of a transiting planet by the
      starlight filtered through it, hunting combinations — oxygen with methane, say — that chemistry should
      not sustain without something alive maintaining the disequilibrium.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Watch the K2-18b story as a lesson in how this works: a dimethyl-sulphide claim in
      2023, headlines, then careful reanalysis showing the signal was far weaker than announced. That cycle is
      not science failing. It is science working, in public, at speed.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate V <span class="spec">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The UAP Record</h3>
      <p>Something genuinely changed after 2017. The Pentagon acknowledged a programme; three Navy videos were
      released and authenticated; the 2021 ODNI preliminary assessment examined 144 incidents and could explain
      one. Congress created AARO. Trained observers with gun-camera footage are a different class of witness
      from a blurry photograph.</p>
      <p>And still: not one recovered artefact, not one unambiguous high-resolution image, no instrumented
      multi-sensor capture that rules out parallax, glare, sensor artefact, drone, balloon or classified
      hardware. The GOFAST object's "impossible speed" dissolves once you do the parallax geometry properly.</p>
      <p>The correct position is uncomfortable and dull: <em>unidentified</em> is a confession of ignorance,
      not a vehicle. Something is in the data. Nothing in the data requires another star.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VI <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Abduction Phenomenon</h3>
      <p>Hundreds of thousands of people sincerely report being taken. The experiences are vivid, consistent,
      profoundly disturbing, and — this matters — generally reported by people with no other sign of mental
      illness. They are not lying and they are not mad.</p>
      <p>There is also a well-mapped neurology here. Sleep paralysis occurs when REM atonia persists into
      waking: the body is immobilised, the threat system is fully online, and the brain hallucinates a presence
      in the room. Around eight percent of people experience it. Add temporal-lobe activity, hypnagogic
      imagery, and the documented capacity of hypnotic regression to manufacture detailed false memories, and
      the anatomy of the classic account is largely accounted for.</p>
      <p class="muted small">This explains the <em>form</em> of the experience. It does not entitle anyone to
      contempt for the people having it, and this order will not extend any. See
      <a href="/neurobiology/">Limb V</a>.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VII <span class="hist">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Visitors Change With the Century</h3>
      <p>The sky people are never quite strangers. Medieval Europe met fairies who stole children and returned
      them disoriented with missing hours. The 1890s produced a wave of mysterious <em>airships</em>, crewed by
      American inventors, in the decade of the airship. 1947 gave us discs, at the dawn of the jet age. The
      1960s began the surgical greys, as clinical medicine entered every home.</p>
      <p>Vallée's observation is the uncomfortable one: the <em>structure</em> — abduction, missing time,
      a message about humanity's fate, the return — is remarkably stable, while the <em>costume</em> tracks the
      technology of the era precisely.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Two readings, both serious. Either the phenomenon is generated by human minds and
      dresses in contemporary clothes, or something real presents itself in whatever idiom the witness can
      receive. Vallée himself leans to the second.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VIII <span class="myth">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Channelled Literature</h3>
      <p>A large body of text claims to transmit non-human intelligence directly: the <em>Law of One</em>
      material (Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty, 1981–84), Bashar, the Pleiadian canon, and a hundred smaller
      streams. The <em>Law of One</em> is the one this order reads most closely — its densities, its service to
      self and service to others, its insistence on free will and non-interference as the governing ethic of
      contact.</p>
      <p>Its claims are not testable, and this page will not pretend otherwise. What can be said is that it is
      internally coherent across five volumes, that it declines to make the falsifiable predictions its
      imitators love, and that it repeatedly instructs the reader to discard anything that does not resonate —
      an unusual move for a text seeking authority.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Read as philosophy and as primary esoteric document. Shelved <span class="myth">◆</span>,
      deliberately and without embarrassment. See the Black Tribunal and Limb VII on the
      <a href="/">Introduction</a>.</p>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

