<!-- ============================== THE LEDGER ============================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Survives Scrutiny</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Planets are common; most stars have them, and small rocky worlds in temperate orbits are abundant.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> The building blocks are everywhere: amino acids in meteorites, complex organics in interstellar clouds and on comets.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Life on Earth appeared remarkably early — within a few hundred million years of the surface becoming habitable.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Subsurface oceans exist on Europa and Enceladus, and Enceladus is venting organics into space for free sampling.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Extremophiles survive conditions once assumed lethal, widening the habitable envelope considerably.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Atmospheric biosignature detection is now technically possible; this is the live frontier.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> A residue of UAP cases, with trained observers and instrument data, is genuinely unexplained.</li>
        <li><span class="hist">◆</span> The encounter narrative is cross-cultural and ancient, whatever is generating it.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> The silence is a real observation requiring a real explanation.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Does Not</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>Ancient astronauts built the pyramids.</strong> We have the quarries, the ramps, the tools, the workers' village, their bread ovens and their pay disputes. The theory's load-bearing assumption is that non-European people could not have done it.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>Roswell was a flying saucer.</strong> The declassified answer — Project Mogul, a high-altitude acoustic balloon array for detecting Soviet tests — is a genuine secret, just not that one.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>The Nazca lines are runways.</strong> Drawn on soft ground that would not support an aircraft, by a culture whose pottery shows the same figures.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>'Oumuamua was a probe.</strong> An odd object, certainly. Natural explanations — a nitrogen-ice shard, a fluffy fractal aggregate — require no new physics and have not been excluded.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>Crop circles.</strong> Bower and Chorley demonstrated the method with a plank and a rope in 1991, after fifteen years of doing it.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>The Face on Mars.</strong> Resolved at higher resolution into an ordinary mesa, as the pareidolia account predicted.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>"The government has the bodies."</strong> Eighty years, four continents, tens of thousands of participants, zero documents, zero defectors with material. The conspiracy is a harder claim than the craft.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small mt-1">Discarding these makes the serious version of the question stronger, not
      weaker. The weak arguments are what let people dismiss the whole subject unexamined.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =========================== HOW TO EVALUATE ============================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Method</p>
    <h2>How to Weigh a Contact Claim</h2>
    <p class="lede">This subject is the single most efficient generator of nonsense in the modern world, and
    also possibly the most important question there is. Both facts demand the same thing: a procedure.</p>

    <details class="scroll" open>
      <summary>1 · Find the primary document</summary>
      <p>Not the documentary, not the book citing the documentary. The original report, the original interview,
      the original sensor file. A startling proportion of famous cases shrink dramatically at this step — the
      detail everybody repeats turns out to have entered the story on its third retelling.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="scroll">
      <summary>2 · Ask what the witness could see from where they stood</summary>
      <p>Most dramatic footage is a distant object against a featureless sky. Without a known range you cannot
      derive size, speed or acceleration — and parallax from a moving camera manufactures impossible motion for
      free. The GOFAST object is the textbook case.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="scroll">
      <summary>3 · Count the inferential steps</summary>
      <p>"I saw a light manoeuvre strangely" is one claim. "Therefore it was a craft, therefore it was not
      human, therefore it came from another star, therefore it is being concealed" is four more, each needing
      its own evidence. Claims are routinely smuggled through as a single package.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="scroll">
      <summary>4 · Check whether the absence of evidence is expected</summary>
      <p>If a claim implies physical traces — metal, radiation, wreckage, bodies, paperwork — then their total
      absence is itself evidence. If it implies nothing checkable at all, it is not a hypothesis. It is a
      position.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="scroll">
      <summary>5 · Notice what you want to be true</summary>
      <p>The hardest step and the one that matters. Nearly everyone in this field, sceptic and believer alike,
      arrived with a wish: for company, for rescue, for meaning, or for a tidy universe with nothing strange in
      it. Name yours before you assess the evidence, or it will do the assessing for you.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

