<!-- ============================== TIMELINE ================================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Lineage</p>
    <h2>A Record of the Question</h2>
    <ul class="timeline">
      <li><span class="when">c. 400 BCE</span> The atomists argue for infinite worlds; Epicurus writes that there must be other earths with other living things.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1584</span> Giordano Bruno publishes on innumerable inhabited worlds. Burned in 1600 — for a broad heresy, not this alone, though it was on the list.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1877</span> Schiaparelli records <em>canali</em> on Mars; mistranslation gives Lowell his canals and the public its first alien civilisation.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1896</span> The American airship wave — mystery craft crewed by inventors, in the decade of the dirigible.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1938</span> Welles broadcasts <em>The War of the Worlds</em>; the panic was smaller than legend, the cultural imprint enormous.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1947</span> Kenneth Arnold sees nine objects near Mount Rainier and describes their motion as like a saucer. The press keeps the noun.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1950</span> Fermi asks his question over lunch at Los Alamos.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1960</span> Drake points a dish at Tau Ceti and Epsilon Eridani. Project Ozma begins the search.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1961</span> The Hill case introduces abduction, missing time and hypnotic regression to the canon.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1974</span> The Arecibo message is transmitted toward M13, arriving in roughly 25,000 years.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1977</span> The Wow! signal. 72 seconds, never repeated.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1981</span> The <em>Law of One</em> sessions begin in Louisville, Kentucky.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1992</span> First confirmed exoplanets, orbiting a pulsar. Three years later, 51 Pegasi b.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1996</span> ALH84001 is announced as Martian fossil life; the structures are later explained abiotically, but astrobiology gets its funding.</li>
      <li><span class="when">2017</span> 'Oumuamua passes through; the Pentagon's AATIP programme is revealed in the press.</li>
      <li><span class="when">2021</span> The ODNI assessment: 144 incidents, one explained.</li>
      <li><span class="when">2022–</span> JWST begins reading exoplanet atmospheres. The biosignature era starts in earnest.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

